{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>For He knows our formation</b> — our origin, and this includes all that He mentioned, for He bears iniquity and transgression and sin, and the word לפניו is lacking, and likewise He remembers it before Him." "And the sense of <b>for we are dust</b> — for the bones are the foundation of the body, and they are cold and dry like the nature of dust."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 103, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:38:02.703569708Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}